--TEST--
A `class<T>` and a `callable` have no implicit string form: after `echo`, around `.` and in an interpolated piece each is `E0707`, and the class reference's help names `as string` (`rule:classes/stringable`)
--FILE--
<?nvs
class Animal {}

class<Animal> $b = 'Animal' as class<Animal>;
echo $b;
echo "a " . $b;
echo "x {$b}";
callable $f = fn(): int => 1;
echo $f;
echo "a " . $f;
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0707]: `class<Animal>` has no string form
%A
5 | echo $b;
%A
  = help: convert it with `as string` to get the class name, as in `$c as string`
%A
error[E0707]: `class<Animal>` has no string form
%A
6 | echo "a " . $b;
%A
error[E0707]: `class<Animal>` has no string form
%A
7 | echo "x {$b}";
%A
error[E0707]: `callable` has no string form
%A
9 | echo $f;
%A
  = help: a function has no text. Call it and use the value it returns
%A
error[E0707]: `callable` has no string form
%A
10 | echo "a " . $f;
%A
error: aborting due to 5 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
